lar</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981143">listeskiljeteikn</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="186_3712_630078"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To change to a newer, and/or more powerful or sophisticated version of a product.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3712">upgrade</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="630078">oppgradere</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18601_650955_1981144"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A calendar that is based on cycles of the moon phase.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650955">Lunar calendar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981144">månekalender</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18604_650958_1981145"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A range in an XML list that has been linked to an element in an XML map.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650958">mapped range</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981145">tilordna område</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18605_650959_1453077"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A shape on a stencil that you use repeatedly to create drawings. When you drag a shape from a stencil onto the drawing page, the shape becomes an instance of that master.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650959">master shape</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1453077">malfigur</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18609_650963_2543308"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A macro containing AddMenu actions that you can use to create a custom menu bar or shortcut menu.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650963">menu bar macro</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2543308">menylinemakro</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18613_650967_2543302"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An editor that is used to add text, edit HTML tags, and edit any Microsoft Visual Basic Scripting Edition (VBScript) code in a data access page. You can also view your page in the Script Editor as it would appear in a Web browser.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650967">Microsoft Script Editor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2543302">Microsoft Script Editor</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18614_650968_1981146"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tone in a picture that is in the middle of the tonal range, between the lightest and darkest tones</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650968">midtone</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981146">mellomtone</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1864_558511_1981079"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An incoming conversation that was not acknowledged by the user. Missed conversation notifications are saved and reported to the user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="558511">missed conversation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></la