ased, data interchange format that is used to transmit structured data, typically in Ajax Web applications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115314">JavaScript Object Notation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540677">JavaScript Object Notation</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24197_1115315_2540418"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The text-based, data interchange format that is used to transmit structured data, typically in Ajax Web applications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115315">JSON</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540418">JSON</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24197_1115315_2540677"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The text-based, data interchange format that is used to transmit structured data, typically in Ajax Web applications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115315">JSON</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540677">JavaScript Object Notation</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24198_1115316_2540419"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An operation that requires more resources than are allowed by a threshold, based on the number of items or amount of information that is processed during the operation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115316">privileged task</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540419">privilegert oppgåve</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2420_308318_631652"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The date after which information or a resource is no longer valid.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="308318">expiration date</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="631652">forfallsdato</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24202_1115320_1981348"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A process, thread, or set of related processes or threads that requires significant system resources or time, or requires exclusive access to large amounts of data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115320">resource-intensive task</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981348">ressursintensiv oppgåve</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24205_1115323_2540420"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An extensible programming model and components that can be used to design and implement custom applications for common business processes, such as document approval. Components include version control, tracking, and reporting.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115323">workflow foundation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540420">arbeidsflytrammeverk</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24206_1115324_2540421"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The object that is used to initiate any actions with the client-side object model. It is the primary entry point for the client object model, and the primary object for coordinating requests against corresponding objects in a site collection.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115324">client context</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540421">klientkontekst</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24207_1115325_2540422"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software component that can be used to connect to a data source, and index and include data from that source in search results.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115325">connector framework</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540422">koplingsrammeverk</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24208_1115326_2540423"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A server-side code routine that is called when a feature is activated, deactivated, installed, uninstalled, or upgraded on a computer, server farm, or server cluster.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115326">feature event receiver</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540423">funksjonshendingsmottakar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24209_1115327_2540424"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A statistic that indicates the degree to which a computer, server farm, or server cluster meets a specific demand for that configuration. It also indicates which log information to copy to a central location for review.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115327">health tracking indicator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540424">indikator for tilstandssporing</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24210_1115328_2540425"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A content type that inherits settings from a base content type that was designed for any type of SharePoint list item.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115328">item-based content type</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540425">elementbasert innhaldstype</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24211_1115329_2540426"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A content type that inherits settings from a base content type that was designed for document libraries.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115329">document-based content type</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540426">dokumentbasert innhaldstype</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24212_1119987_1981352"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A custom solution that can be deployed to a site by a site collection administrator, without approval from the farm administrator. Without that approval, the solution has full access to the immediate site and restricted access to system resources and other sites.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1119987">sandboxed solution</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981352">sandkasseløysing</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24213_1115331_2540427"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A persistent container that defines and stores instructions for a job to be run on a server, server farm, or server cluster. To run, a job must have an associated job definition, and a definition must be associated with a service or a Web application.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115331">job definition</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540427">jobbdefinisjon</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24214_1115332_2540428"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A dedicated, administrator-level user account that performs scheduled administrative tasks.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115332">timer account</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540428">timerkonto</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24215_1115333_2540429"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A compressed file that can be deployed to a server farm or a site. It can contain assemblies, resource files, site and feature definitions, templates, code access security policies, and Web Parts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115333">solution package</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540429">løysingpakke</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24216_1115334_1981349"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A custom keyword or description and shortcut to a Web page or item on a SharePoint site or the Internet. All of these tags can be viewed, managed, and shared by using My Site.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115334">social tag</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981349">sosialmerke</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24217_1115335_1981350"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of features that can be used to store and share comments, shortcuts, descriptions, and other information about Web pages and items on a SharePoint site or the Internet.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115335">social data</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981350">sosialdata</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24218_1115336_2540430"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A reserved time for performing administrative tasks on a computer, server farm, or server cluster.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115336">service window</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540430">servicevindauge</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24219_1115337_2540431"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An administrative setting that limits the number of query results for SharePoint lists, sites, and site collections that contain a large number of items.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115337">query-size threshold</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540431">terskel for spørjingsresultat</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24220_1115338_2540432"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A reserved time for performing large, resource-intensive queries for a computer, server farm, or server cluster.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115338">query window</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540432">spørjingsvindauge</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24221_1115339_2540433"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A solution package that contains only a DLL that stores localized versions of strings in another solution package. After a language pack is deployed to a site, users can display the corresponding user interface in that language.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115339">language pack</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540433">språkpakke</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24222_1115340_2540434"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An area for storing comments about a Web page. A note board can appear on a Web page or in a separate dialog box. The notes can be viewed, managed, and shared by using My Site.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115340">note board</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540434">notatområde</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24223_1115341_2540435"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft SQL Server, MSDE, or WMSDE database that stores health monitoring and usage data temporarily, and can be used for reporting and diagnostics.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115341">logging database</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540435">loggdatabase</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24224_1115342_1981351"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A statistic that indicates the degree to which a computer, server farm, or server cluster meets usage demands for that configuration.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1115342">quality-of-service indicator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981351">indikator for tenestekvalitet</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24245_1117153_1522339"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An installation package that the user downloads from http://download.live.com/?mkt=en-us.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1117153">download</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1522339">nedlasting</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24247_1117155_1375768"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The main landing or start page on Windows Live.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1117155">Windows Live Home</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1375768">Windows Live Heim</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2425_34681_630295"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A predefined set of harmonized colors that you can apply to text and objects. Text and objects with an applied scheme color will change automatically when you switch to a new color scheme or modify the current color scheme.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="34681">color scheme</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="630295">fargeval</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24254_1117166_2769642"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A device that connects networks using the same communications protocols so that information can be passed from one to the other.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1117166">bridge</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2769642">bru</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24287_1119142_1650479"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The button next to a search box that someone clicks to search for something.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1119142">Search button</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig>