one calls. Users must be signed in to Windows Live Messenger to use it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1136281">Windows Live Call</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1375783">Windows Live Telefon</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24607_1136282_1375784"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows Live service that lets people and groups add, manage, and share event information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1136282">Windows Live Calendar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1375784">Windows Live Kalender</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24608_1136283_1375785"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows Live service that notifies someone of an event or information based on their subscription preferences. The alerts can be sent to Messenger, Mail, Hotmail, or a mobile device.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1136283">Windows Live Alerts</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1375785">Windows Live Varslingar</term><termNote type="geographica