ticles, device drivers, Help files, and other support files you can download from Microsoft.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1508820">MSDL</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540470">MSDL</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29472_1508822_2540471"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A style sheet that contains formatting rules, and that is referenced by an XML file to which the rules are applied. The standard set of rules for XML stylesheets is the Extensible Style Language (XSL).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1508822">XML stylesheet</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540471">XML-stilark</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29473_1508823_1981543"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An administrative tool that examines a computer, server farm, or server cluster and provides statistics that indicate the degree to which the configuration meets expected demands.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1508823">health analyzer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981543">verktøy for tilstandsanalyse</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29474_1508825_1981545"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A custom handler that calls and runs custom code during the creation process for a site.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1508825">site provisioning provider</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981545">nettstadklargjeringsleverandør</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29475_1508827_2540472"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The representation of graphic objects such as lines, arcs, and squares by using geometrical formulas. By contrast, bitmapped graphics (also called raster graphics) are stored as a collection of pixels.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1508827">vector graphics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540472">vektorgrafikk</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29476_1508830_1981547"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Microsoft Office program that you can use to organize related documents. You can check spelling, number pages consecutively across all documents in the binder, and print the documents.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1508830">Binder</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981547">Dokumentordnar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29477_1508834_2540474"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A text string used in HTML to identify a page element's type, format, and appearance. Many elements have start and end tags that define where the element starts and stops.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1508834">HTML tag</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540474">HTML-kode</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29480_1508864_1981548"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A contiguous piece of text or string of characters sharing the same attributes. All characters in a run have the same directional properties.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1508864">run</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981548">tekststreng med like attributta</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29481_1508936_1981549"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A reading order and alignment setting that is commonly used in controls that display text. When you select the Context setting, the reading order is determined by the first strong character (not a numeral or special character) that you type.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1508936">Context</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981549">kontekst</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29483_1508938_1981550"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In an outline, to change a heading to body text or to a lower heading level: for example, to change from Heading 5 to Heading 6.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1508938">demote</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981550">senke</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29491_1509011_1646928"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A demonstration of a product or service that a customer interacts with to see how features work.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1509011">demo</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1646928">demo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29491_1509011_1646959"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A demonstration of a product or service that a customer interacts with to see how features work.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1509011">demo</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1646959">interaktiv demo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29491_1509012_1646928"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A demonstration of a product or service that a customer interacts with to see how features work.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1509012">interactive demo</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1646928">demo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29491_1