irst-party Windows app for playing commercial and homemade DVD-Video discs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2259501">Windows DVD Player</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2260629">DVD-spelar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38860_2259501_2260631"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The first-party Windows app for playing commercial and homemade DVD-Video discs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2259501">Windows DVD Player</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2260631">Windows DVD-spelar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38866_2259535_2260665"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The variable default lock screen image that shows beautiful images on lock combined with hotspots containing fun facts, Windows tips/trick, and more. Users can switch from this default lock screen to a personal picture.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2259535">Windows spotlight</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2260665">Windows-søkjelys</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38879_2259611_2434733"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To add a shortcut to an application or part of an application or contact by fixing its tile to the Start screen (the full screen view of Start) or Start menu.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2259611">pin to Start</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2434733">feste til Start</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3888_25223_630215"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A communication line used for data transfer among the components of a computer system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="25223">bus</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="630215">buss</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38880_2259632_2260652"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In the Windows Store for Business and Education Store, to get apps and other digital goods into the hands of employees or students.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2259632">distribute</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2260652">distribuere</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38882_2259634_2260649"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that lets customers extend their gaming experience across multiple devices, play with other users, and show off scores and achievements.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2259634">game hub</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2260649">spelhub</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38883_2259635_2260634"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The default browser in Windows 10, which provides a more interoperable, reliable, and discoverable experience with advanced features including the ability to annotate on web pages, a distraction-free reading experience, and integration of Cortana. Also available on iOS and Android.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2259635">Microsoft Edge</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2260634">Microsoft Edge</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><t