 one-time purchase, without any major feature updates.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2929998">Office LTSC</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2931666">Office LTSC</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52032_2929999_2947277"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The New Zealand holiday celebrated on February 6 that commemorates the signing of the Treaty of Waitangi in 1840, signed by representatives of the British Crown and Maori chiefs and often considered to be New Zealand's founding document.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2929999">Waitangi Day</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2947277">Waitangi-dagen</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52033_2930000_2947278"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The day on which Waitangi Day is celebrated if the official holiday itself falls on a weekend.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2930000">Waitangi Day Bank Holiday</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2947278">Offentleg fridag (Waitangi-dagen)</term><termNote type