a computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="49777">serial port</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="630431">COM-port</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9331_49777_630432"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A serial communications port used to connect a device, such as a modem, printer, or mobile device, to a computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="49777">serial port</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="630432">kommunikasjonsport</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9331_49777_630433"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A serial communications port used to connect a device, such as a modem, printer, or mobile device, to a computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="49777">serial port</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="630433">seriell port</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9332_210450_1980901"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The formal name for Excel 12 file format. The Excel XML Format has an open, royalty-free specification, and is the technology licensed to external parties.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="210450">Excel XML Format</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1980901">Excel XML-format</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9334_397201_1796701"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of object that has an email address on a domain in the organization, but the object does not have a mailbox in the domain at which to receive messages. The object appears in the global address list, which allows other people in the organization to easily locate or send a message to that person, but the administrator does not need to manage an unnecessary mailbox. Contacts, users, and even folders can be mail-enabled.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397201">mail-enabled object</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1796701">e-postobjekt</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9336_119369_630856"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A database object that stores data in records (rows) and fields (columns). The data is usually about a particular category of things, such as employees or orders.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="119369">table</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="630856">tabell</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="934_76743_630609"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A distinctive symbol that identifies a person, business, or organization.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="76743">logo</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="630609">logo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9340_148449_2540250"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An image map that passes the coordinates of the mouse pointer to a CGI handler routine on the server. Server-side image maps require the Web server to compute the target URL of the hyperlink based on the mouse pointer coordinates.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="148449">server-side image map</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540250">biletkart på tenarsida</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9344_136605_630954"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of CD on which files can be copied, erased, and replaced.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="136605">compact disc-rewritable</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="630954">omskrivbar CD</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9344_136605_630955"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of CD on which files can be copied, erased, and replaced.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="136605">compact disc-rewritable</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="630955">CD-RW</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9344_136606_630954"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of CD on which files can be copied, erased, and replaced.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="136606">CD-RW</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="630954">omskrivbar CD</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9344_136606_630955"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of CD on which files can be copied, erased, and replaced.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="136606">CD-RW</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="630955">CD-RW</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9355_309006_1207239"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The legal agreement between Microsoft and the user, with regard to the terms of use and transfer of software.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="309006">Microsoft Software License Terms</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1207239">lisensvilkår for Microsoft-programvare</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9362_186059_2545783"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to a call that is free for the initiator to use.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="186059">toll-free</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2545783">grønt nummer</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9364_180296_1980833"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Unsolicited commercial instant messages or presence subscription requests sent to multiple users.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="180296">Spim</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1980833">nettsøppel (i direktemelding)</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9375_85176_630669"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">For local area networks (LANs), a device that is connected to the network and is capable of communicating with other network devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="85176">node</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="630669">node</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9376_207701_228083"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A document format that displays a page exactly as the author intended, independent of the viewer's screen size or window size, dots per inch (dpi), available fonts, or any other system-specific settings. The page renders the same on any compatible device, ensuring a consistent experience for all users.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="207701">fixed document</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="228083">fast dokument</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="938_584283_1981090"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A bar chart subtype that shows the relationship of individual items to the whole.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="584283">stacked bar chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981090">stabla liggjande stolpediagram</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9386_105576_2540171"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A server-based user profile that is downloaded to the local computer when a user logs on and that is updated both locally and on the server when the user logs off.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="105576">roaming user profile</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540171">sentral brukarprofil</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9386_503125_2540171"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A server-based user profile that is downloaded to the local computer when a user logs on and that is updated both locally and on the server when the user logs off.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="503125">roaming profile</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2540171">sentral brukarprofil</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9389_185000_1980859"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A button on Audio Controls that mutes the user's microphone.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="185000">Mute Microphone</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1980859">Demp mikrofon</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9391_318770_630354"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The † character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318770">DAGGER</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="630354">kross</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9391_42062_630354"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The † character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="42062">dagger</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="630354">kross</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9392_60785_1538575"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An information structure that precedes and identifies the information that follows.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="60785">header</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1538575">hode</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9394_144700_1207240"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Used by Microsoft Exchange to identify, locate, and open a form.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="144700">message class</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1207240">meldingsklasse</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9396_303757_1206053"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A function of some Web browsers that allows users to surf and view multiple pages by loading Web sites into sections (or tabs) of one page, rather than multiple pages.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="303757">tabbed browsing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1206053">fanebasert nettlesing</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9398_185340_1980871"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A selection that displays the first and last name, instead of the email address or sign-in name, for each contact in the user's Contacts list.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="185340">Show Friendly Name</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1980871">Vis eigendefinert namn</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9399_186186_1980893"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A notification bar warning the user about data that is blocked in the loaded file. Trust Bars can be for information only (non-actionable) or actionable.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="186186">Trust Bar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1980893">klareringsfelt</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="94_397174_1796675"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A mail-enabled Active Directory user that represents a user outside the Exchange organization. Each mail user has an external email address. A mail user is similar to a mail contact, except that a mail user has Active Directory logon credentials and can access resources.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397174">mail user</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="nn-NO"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1796675">e-postbrukar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NOR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="940_39810_630340"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A processor that performs additional functions or assists the CPU.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="39810">coprocessor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular<